WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.868
-It is great to see you.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.036
Welcome back to
"The Tonight Show," bud.

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.470
-Thank you, man.
I'm so excited to see people.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.938
-Yeah, it's amazing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:08.007
They're so excited to see you.

00:00:08.007 --> 00:00:09.442
You look great, buddy.

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.511
-Oh, you know what?
The pandemic, man.

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:14.279
Let me tell you,
I lost 70 pounds.

00:00:14.279 --> 00:00:15.881
-Holy -- good for you.

00:00:15.881 --> 00:00:17.250
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.552
People ask me all the time,
"What's your secret?"

00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:20.753
I said, "It's no secret.

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:22.255
They closed
all the restaurants."

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.856
[ Laughter ]
-They just closed it down.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:26.359
-And I'm still wearing the same
shirt that I was wearing

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.727
when I was still
70 pounds heavier

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.495
because I plan to eat again.

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:30.697
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:33.065
The last time
you were on our show,

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:34.466
you looked sharp, buddy.

00:00:34.466 --> 00:00:35.769
But here's you backstage.

00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:38.671
-Oh. [ Laughs ]
-Yeah, look at that.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.173
-It's rare to see you in a suit.

00:00:41.173 --> 00:00:44.043
-The one and only time
I ever wore a suit

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:46.813
was on your show,
because the time before that,

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.481
I was wearing shorts,
and I heard you

00:00:48.481 --> 00:00:50.516
make a comment about,
"Thanks for dressing up."

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:51.817
And I'm like, "Uuuugh."

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:53.252
And my family saw the show,
and they were like...

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:55.321
[ Speaking,
swearing in Spanish ]

00:00:58.223 --> 00:00:59.659
And I'm like, "All right, look,
I get it, I get it."

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.861
-Yeah, exactly right.
-You know what she's saying.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:02.929
-[ Laughing ]
-You know what she's saying.

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.230
-Something around that, yeah.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.465
-So I says, "When I come back --
if I get invited back --"

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:09.302
I go, "I'm gonna go all out,
and I'm gonna wear a suit."

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:11.337
And put the picture up again?

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:12.938
I had a little bit of an issue.

00:01:12.938 --> 00:01:16.609
This is your wardrobe area,
and these two --

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:19.078
You know, I think
they still work here.

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:20.713
-Yes.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.648
-Apparently, what happened is,

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:25.051
I had a wardrobe
malfunction, okay?

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.552
Yeah, because I never
wore pants.

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:28.220
Clearly, I did it today.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.556
But the pant leg ripped.

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:33.493
And so, you know, I was
bringing sexy back that day.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:35.061
And --
-Before the show?

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.829
-As you were getting ready
to introduce me.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.264
And so, we had
to stop everything,

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.700
and I had to go in the back,
and they had to sew it up

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.702
and fix me up
and tape me together.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.436
I mean, look at me right --
I don't wear --

00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:47.540
Some people wear suits,
and they look nice, okay?

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.809
And some look like
affordable lawyers.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:52.178
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:53.178
-No, no, no, no.

00:01:53.178 --> 00:01:54.647
You look -- Come on.
-Eh?

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.116
-No, no, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.252
-A low budget secret service guy
right there.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.720
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:03.022
I don't know how he got shot.
-Yeah!

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.590
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.260
I almost want to say,
"Look at you now,"

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.631
because you're going to be
performing at Dodger Stadium --

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.500
the first comedian ever
to perform at Dodger Stadium.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.201
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.201 --> 00:02:17.903
It's already sold out.

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:20.439
You're adding, like, another
second show or something.

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:22.775
This is an audience
of 40,000 people.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.510
-I know, I'm like
the Bad Bunny of comedy.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.178
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:27.780
-Are you excited about this?
-He's a "Fluffy Bunny."

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.849
It's -- It's --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:32.685
If we ever do a collab,
it's gonna be perfect.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.088
Fluffy Bad Bunny, yeah.
-Fluffy Bad Bunny, yeah.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:37.223
-It's surreal,
because it's like, you know,

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.425
whenever I tell people
I'm doing Dodger Stadium,

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.659
they're like, "Well, what --
are you singing

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:41.827
the national anthem?

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:43.095
Are you cleaning it?

00:02:43.095 --> 00:02:44.230
What are you doing?"

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:45.498
And I'm like,
"No, I'm performing."

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.767
They're like, "Do they have,
like, a small room?"

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:51.571
It's like the Super Bowl
for a comedian, you know?

00:02:51.571 --> 00:02:52.839
-Yeah, of course it is.

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:54.473
-And not everybody gets
to play the Super Bowl,

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:56.742
so I feel very fortunate
that it's happening,

00:02:56.742 --> 00:02:58.010
and it's happening
in my hometown.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.246
And, yeah, it's already --
-Well done, buddy.

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.947
You put the work in,
and, man, you're funny.

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:03.849
It's gonna be great.
Congratulations on that.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:06.152
That's a dream come true.
That's beyond a dream.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.787
How could you even
dream about that?

00:03:08.787 --> 00:03:11.557
-Yeah, you know, you say,

00:03:11.557 --> 00:03:13.326
"How can you dream
of something like that?"

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.527
Because people ask me
all the time,

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.362
"Did you ever think that
it could get this big?"

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:19.031
And I'm like, "No,
my only goal in life

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:21.033
when I first started
doing standup was,

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.668
I just wanted to pay my rent."

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.236
-Yeah.
-Because people always say,

00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:26.105
"Reach for the stars."

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:29.441
It's unrealistic.

00:03:29.441 --> 00:03:30.676
You what I'm saying?
I tell people,

00:03:30.676 --> 00:03:32.444
"Reach for the second floor."

00:03:32.444 --> 00:03:33.879
[ Laughter ]
-You might be able --

00:03:33.879 --> 00:03:35.681
-Yeah, and this way,
if you end up on the roof,

00:03:35.681 --> 00:03:36.749
you are an overachiever.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:38.851
-That's exactly correct, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.920
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:45.057
-You're going to debut something
exclusively just for us tonight.

00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:47.526
What's your story behind these?

00:03:47.526 --> 00:03:49.762
-So, a couple years ago,

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:52.432
I started this
beautiful relationship

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:54.200
with a company called Funko.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:57.103
And Funko has these Pop figures,
and basically,

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.237
they're the hottest thing
out there.

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.106
Every year at Comic-Con,
I-i mean, you know,

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.874
millions of these figures
have been sold.

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:05.344
And when I approached them
to see if there was interest

00:04:05.344 --> 00:04:07.447
in having a comedian Pop,
they were like,

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:10.015
"Well, we don't have a category
for comedians."

00:04:10.015 --> 00:04:12.017
And I'm like,
"Well, maybe we can start one."

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:15.622
And next thing I know,
we made a little deal,

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.656
and they came out
with a figure for me.

00:04:17.656 --> 00:04:18.657
-It's sold out.

00:04:18.657 --> 00:04:21.527
-Yes, I've sold a lot of those.

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:24.163
-Yeah, a lot.
-A lot, a lot. [ Laughs ]

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:25.665
-A lot.
-Thank you, Funko.

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:28.767
But to commemorate
the Dodger Stadium show,

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:32.705
Funko made me a special one
specifically for Dodger Stadium,

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:33.973
and it comes out this week.

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:35.742
And this is the first time
anyone's gonna see it.

00:04:35.742 --> 00:04:37.943
-Here we go. Quest, can I get
a little drum roll, please?

00:04:37.943 --> 00:04:39.912
[ Drum roll ]

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:42.214
Ladies and gentlemen...

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:44.016
Stadium Fluffy.

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:46.185
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:49.055
-Look at this.
Stadium Fluffy.

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:52.525
[ Laughter ]
Come on!

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.160
Congratulations, buddy.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.361
Couldn't happen
to a better guy, man.

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:56.395
-Thank you.

00:04:56.395 --> 00:04:58.197
-Gabriel Iglesias, everybody.

00:04:58.197 --> 00:05:00.600
Go see him perform
at Dodger Stadium

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.702
May 6th and 7th.

